  "content": "\n                    <div class=\"plugin-tabmeta-details\"><div class=\"table-wrap\"></div></div><p><span class=\"inline-comment-marker\" data-ref=\"7de81ae6-92e3-453a-9203-90258f609c48\"><br></span></p><div class=\"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-information\"><span class=\"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-information-macro-icon\"></span><div class=\"confluence-information-macro-body\"><p>OBE Revocation will be integrated with the ongoing \"Misbehavior Authority Integration\" sub project as SCMS <abbr title=\"Proof-Of-Concept\">POC</abbr> release 2.0. Until then every reported pseudonym certificate leads automatically to a revocation of all pseudonym certificates belonging to this OBE for testing purposes.</p></div></div><h2 id=\"UseCase8:OBEPseudonymCertificateRevocation-Goals\"><span class=\"inline-comment-marker\" data-ref=\"7de81ae6-92e3-453a-9203-90258f609c48\">Goals</span></h2><p><span class=\"inline-comment-marker\" data-ref=\"9775adee-7724-4b4f-8e1b-647d143b895a\">Perform misbehavior investigation and eventually revocation of OBEs</span>.</p>\n                    ",
